  "summary": "Host identity exfiltration to hardcoded webhook on install and require",
  "details": "The package executes the `id` command and sends the installer's hostname together with the command output (username, uid, gid, groups) to the hardcoded endpoint https://blue-comet-66.webhook.cool via an HTTPS GET request with query parameters. This exfiltration is triggered automatically by `scripts.postinstall` (`node beacon.js postinstall`) during `npm install`, and again from `index.js` when the package is loaded via `require()`/`import`. beacon.js reads `os.hostname()` and runs `execSync('id')`, then invokes `https.get` with `host` and `id_output` query parameters against the hardcoded webhook URL.",
